# `@jesscss/less-parser`

- **Role**: LESS parsing built atop core + css-parser.
- **Build**: `cd packages/less-parser && pnpm build`
- **Tests**: `cd packages/less-parser && pnpm test`

## ⛔ Node shapes = the Chevrotain productions

`src/grammar.ts` + `src/builders.ts` (parseman) are a 1:1 port of the legacy Chevrotain parser.
**The authoritative spec for every AST node shape is `src/productions/*.ts`** (`root.ts`, `values.ts`,
`selectors.ts`, `guards.ts`). Before changing a builder to "fix" a node shape, READ the matching
production and reproduce it exactly. Never guess the shape from grammar text, parseman output, or
test expectations, and never invent "grammar bug"/"partial accessor" explanations for a mismatch.
See `.cursor/rules/domains/parsers.mdc` for the full rule.

## Note (repo anomaly)

`packages/less-parser/vitest.config.ts` imports `../../vitest.config.js`, but the repo root contains `vitest.config.ts` (no `.js` found). Keep this in mind if test config resolution behaves oddly.

